# Local build tooling for the README. build_readme.py reassembles README.md from
# .scratch/ and asserts every patch it applies; without those inputs it aborts,
# so committing it would ship a script that cannot run. The README itself is
# edited directly - this is scaffolding, not part of the repository.
/build_readme.py
.scratch/
/validate_readme.py
# A stray __pycache__ is easy to create by hand while poking at the validator,
# and a committed .pyc can be loaded in preference to the source it came from.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
